      "title": "Novel Type of Phase Transition in a System of Self-Driven Particles",
      "abstract": "A simple model with a novel type of dynamics is introduced in order to investigate the emergence of self-ordered motion in systems of particles with biologically motivated interaction. In our model particles are driven with a constant absolute velocity and at each time step assume the average direction of motion of the particles in their neighborhood with some random perturbation ($\\eta$) added. We present numerical evidence that this model results in a kinetic phase transition from no transport (zero average velocity, $| {\\bf v}_a | =0$) to finite net transport through spontaneous symmetry breaking of the rotational symmetry. The transition is continuous since $| {\\bf v}_a |$ is found to scale as $(\\eta_c-\\eta)^\\beta$ with $\\beta\\simeq 0.45$.",
